xnu 0459: does the pbl read the bhi doorbell at all

Measured 2026-11-26: the chip's BHI block is initialized (version 1.2, serial,
hwid, exec_env 0) and the MHI reset bit is accepted and cleared, so the boot
ROM executes, but the doorbell written afterwards is never consumed and
BHI_STATUS stays 0. Every host register matches the donor's working SM8475
port, so the question is now whether the ROM starts the fetch at all.

Point the BHI image address at 0x0bad0000, outside the wired SMMU window but
inside this SID's stage-2 translation, and sample CB_FSR/FAR/GFSR around the
doorbell. A translation fault with FAR=0xbad0000 proves the ROM consumed the
doorbell and its fetch reached the SMMU; an unchanged fault record proves the
fetch never started. The same dump reads the PCIe capability's Device Control,
which the donor programs to 0x0810 and this port never touches.

